  "findings": [
    "Aligning 3h source lifetimes reduces SAMPLES bucket rows from 113760 to86688 and marks from446 to340 while series count and samples stay identical to prior staggered R01 fixture. It is a held-out different physical layout, not an independent production workload.",
    "pod broad1d native vs SQL p50 70.2ms vs35.2005ms (1.9943x); CPU114.96175ms vs41.30225ms, selected marks both233.",
    "pod broad3d native vs SQL p50 90.582ms vs43.3975ms (2.0873x); CPU174.0065ms vs58.076ms, selected marks both233.",
    "node broad3d native vs SQL1.1846x on aligned vs1.474x staggered; other broad cases show smaller but positive gains, so impact is metric/timing dependent.",
    "Six baseline A/A control drifts under2.33%, all 18 strict separate native-vs-SQL grid parity tests passed, none hidden by errors.",
    "No additional TAGS or SAMPLES physical index. SQL gains cannot be assigned to fewer marks; the critical path includes native AdaptiveBucketMergingSource, MergeTreeSelect and Expressions, but work_us profiles are not exclusive CPU and cannot alone prove patch safety."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Second independent Github-hosted runner: ratios compare only within each run. Do not pool absolute p50 across the two runners or assert synthetic sample size generalizes to production.",
    "No NaN, staleness marker, duplicate/repeated samples, arbitrary PromQL operator, native histograms, workload HPA, concurrent clients, byte-level query cache, or source C++ planner integration.",
    "Sample-age lifetime fixed3h, short 3d retention; 14d Jenkins canonical metric query still separate. Cannot claim production benefit.",
    "Only query memory peak proven; process allocator RSS is not measured as a fresh-process matched delta."
  ],
  "next_gate": "Source/math proof of eligibility subset and direct adversarial repeated/NaN/stale-marker query outputs. Treat discrepancies as falsifiers. Avoid C++ builds until exact semantics and O2 production allocator cost gate."
